 @Hotobu  "The chips for these cards have been in production < 2 months"
Considering that Nvidia and their AIB partners have had to test them over several months in order to design coolers, and that the rate at which wafers can be built is limited, this is extremely unlikely. Do you think that Samsung converted their entire wafer production line over to Ampere or something?

These dies will have been in mass production for closer to half a year, to build up a stockpile and refine the process to the extent that enough top-tier dies are available.

